guide~
{c---------------------------------------------------------------------------{x
Welcome to Haven of the Embraced.  This is a world loosely based on the
World of Darkness by White Wolf.  You will see many things during your stay
here, and there are some things you will need to know.  Below is a list of
pages that are contained within this book.  To read a page type 'look page#'
i.e.: {Clook page1{x
{c---------------------------------------------------------------------------{x
Table of Contents
 
{MPage1 {x- About Your Character
{MPage2 {x- Getting Started
{MPage3 {x- Freebies
{MPage4 {x- Items and Equipment
{MPage5 {x- Communicating on Haven
{MPage6 {x- Skills and Prayers
{MPage7 {x- Clans, Tribes, Traditions
{MPage8 {x- Immortals and Administration
{MPage9 {x- Haven's Rules
{MPageA {x- Message Boards
{MPageB {x- Frequently Asked Questions
~
E
page1~
About Your Character
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
At any time you wish to see the list of commands available
to your character, simply type '{Ccommands{x' ({WBe sure to type{x
{Wthe entire word, including the '{Ys{W'){x  This will give you a
listing of all commands on Haven.  Be aware that some of
the commands will not be available for use unless you meet
certain requirements.

By typing {Cscore{x, you will be shown a detailed report
of your character's basic statistics.  Useful information,
such as your health, gold, level, etc., will be displayed
for your perusal.

At any time, you can use the {Chelp{x menus, by simply typing
{Chelp <command here>{x.  For example, {Chelp score{x will show
you a help file on the 'score' command.  {Y*We are currently{x
{Yin the process of updating and adding help files.*{x

The {Cwho{x command will show you a list of players who are
currently visible to you on Haven.  Some players may be
invisible, or otherwise hidden from sight.
 
Another useful command is {Carea{x, which shows a list of
areas on Haven, and a general level range for those areas.
This can help you judge proper areas to explore.

Using {Cscan{x, you will glance at rooms adjacent to you and
see any visible enemies or players there.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page2~
Getting Started
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
By using the 'Look' command, you can see what is in a room.
The look command can also be used to look at an object, or
a person.  ex: {C'look'{x, '{Clook knife{x', '{Clook (playername){x'
 
Another command that is as useful as look, is 'examine'
by using this you can take a closer look at an item, or
player. 'examine book' 'examine (playername)'
 
There are 6 movement commands available to you. They are
'{Cnorth{x' '{Csouth{x' '{Ceast{x' '{Cwest{x' '{Cup{x' and '{Cdown{x' Use these
commands to move around Haven.
 
The '{Ckill{x' command will be one of the commands that you 
use the most. It allows you to attempt to kill a monster.
The kill command can also be used to attack a player,
though this isn't recommeded at this time, type 'help pk'
for more information on our rules for player killing.
If you have any questions about it, feel free to ask an
immortal.
 
One of the most common sights in Haven is a corpse.
If you die, your corpse will be in the place that you
died at. You will need to go and retrieve anything from
your corpse. This is where the '{Cget{x' command comes in,
'{Cget all corpse{x' will get everything that you can see from
the corpse you are looting. '{Cget (item) corpse{x' will get
just a particular item from a corpse. The get command will
also allow you to pick up something that might be lying on
the ground.
 
After you have read the Newbie Guide, the best thing for
you to do, is to go through Newbie Training School, so that
you become more familiar with the commands that you will be
using.
 
After you have completed Newbie Training School, the
next area that you will find yourself in is Vantage Point.
Use this area to gain some experience before moving on.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page3~
Freebies
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
Once you have finished your 'Creation Process' to flesh
out your character (or have used one of the three starter
templates), you will be supplied with 15 Freebie Points
to spend at your leisure.  Aside from your initial creation,
these points will be your main source of advancement for
your character here on Haven of the Embraced.  All of the
Statistics that you find on your Character Sheet ({Ccs{x, {Ccs2{x,
and {Ccs3{x) are all increased via these Freebie Points.

Using the {Cfreebie{x command, you are able to bring up the
Freebie Cost screen for your character.  The costs of
increasing the different sections of your character sheet
are shown.  All characters will see the costs for common
statistics found among all characters (Attributes, Abilities,
Willpower, just to name a few), but you will also see any
costs for stats that are specific to your character's race
(Disciplines, Spheres, etc.).  Your current Freebie Points
are also listed here for convenience.

In order to gain additional Freebie Points to advance your
character, you must level up to Level 100.  Once you have
reached Level 100, you have the option to 'remort' to
become more powerful.  This resets your character level
down to level 1, but increases your Freebie Points by 3.
Freebies do not need to be spent immediately, and can be
saved up to purchase more expensive upgrades as needed.
See {yhelp remort{x for additional information on remorts.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page4~
Items and Equipment
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
You will start out with a few pieces of equipment. Type
'{Cequipment{x' to see what you are currently wear{xing. Also
type '{Cinventory{x' to see what you are currently carrying.
 
To wear a particular piece of equipment, use the '{Cwear{x'
command.  Example: '{Cwear dagger{x' '{Cwear all{x'
 
To {Cremove{x a piece of equipment use the 'remove' command.
Example : 'remove dagger' 'remove all'
 
On occassion, you might not be able to remove a particular
piece of equipment, this might be because the item is 
cursed, in which case you might want to visit a healer, or
convince someone to help you remove the curse upon the item.
 
You will find various pieces of equipment throughout your
travels, sometimes they will be weaker than what you might
currently be wearing, sometimes they might be stronger
than what you are currently wearing. You can only wear
equipment that is equal to your current level or lower.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page5~
Communication on Haven
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
There are a variety of ways in which you can communicate
on Haven.
 
OOC : is the Out of Character chat channel, this is used
for general chat, and has absolutely nothing to do with
any Roleplaying aspect of your character. The command for
OOC is 'ooc (texthere)'
OOC is broadcast to everyone on the mud.
 
GOSSIP : This channel is for In Character chat, it is used
for the Roleplaying aspect of your character. The command
for GOSSIP is 'gossip (texthere)'
GOSSIP is also broadcast to everyone on the mud.
 
SAY : This is another of the In Character chat channels,
that you may use in roleplaying your character.
SAY will only be shown to those who are in the same room
as you are. The command for SAY is 'say (texthere)'
 
OSAY : This is much like the SAY command except that it is
for out of charcter chatting to people in the same room as
you are. The command for OSAY is 'osay (texthere)'
 
TELL : This command is used to send a private message to
another person. The TELL channel is an out of character
channel. The command for TELL is, 'tell (person) (text)'
 
Other channels available to you are SHOUT and YELL. Shout
will send a message to all players who are awake in the 
world. Yell will send a message to all awake players in
the same area as you are.
 
By typing 'channel' you will see a list of channels that
are available to you. For help on a particular channel
type 'help (channelhere)'
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page6~
Skills and Prayers
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
Typing 'skills' will show you a list of skills that you 
have at your current level.  By typing 'skills all', you
can see a list of your acquired skills, and what level
they are accessed.
 
Spells are known as prayers on Haven. By typing 'prayer'
you will be shown a list of prayers that are available to
you. By typing 'prayer all' you will be shown a list of 
the prayers you have learned, and what level the prayer
is able to be used.
 
Your ability in a particular skill or prayer is respresented
with a percentage.  This percentage has a small chance of
increasing upon usage, whether it is successful for not.
There are some skills that are considered "always on",
such as 'second attack' or 'enhanced speed', and have the
chance to increase upon triggering.
 
In order to gain new skills and prayers, you must increase
the portions of your character found on your Character
Sheet.  Refer to the Freebies page of this guide for
additional information.  Using the {Cskillmap{x command
will give you a list of all skills in Haven, along with the
corresponding character sheet statistic and dot level
needed to learn the skill or prayer.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page7~
Clans, Tribes, Traditions
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
The different 'races' of Haven have a variety of affiliations
available, depending on which type of character you are
playing.  Each is unique, with its own pool of powers for
you to have access to.
 
Vampires begin the game as a member of a clan, selected
during character creation.  See {yhelp clans{x for additional
information on clans.

Werewolf Tribes are more akin to an adopted family.  A
werewolf must be inducted into one of the tribes by a
senior member of that specific Tribe.  See {yhelp tribes{x
for more information.

Mages must be Awakened into a specific Tradition by a
senior member of that Tradition.  See {yhelp traditions{x
for Tradition information.

At this time, there are no specific affiliations for general
humans.  A human can become embraced into a clan by a
vampire, inducted into a tribe by a werewolf, or inducted
into a tradition by a mage.  In this respect, a normal
basic human has a multitude of options to advance.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page8~
Immortals and Administration
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
Anyone who is above level 100, is an immortal, they are the
builders and administration of the mud. If you need any
assistiance please feel free to look for them, or use the
OOC channel to ask for one. Immortals are here to help as
well as work on Haven to make it a better place.

You can also use the {Cplead{x command to attempt to contact
an immortal who is logged in at the time.
 
The {Cwizlist{x command will give the most current list of
active Immortals.

If you are looking to apply for a position on the immortal
staff, please read the application that is located under
'{chelp application{x'.  Answer the questions and write the
required descriptions, then send them to the Immortals as
instructed in the helpfile.  To be considered for an Immortal
position, you must have played at least 10 hours.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
page9~
Haven's Rules
{c------------------------------------------------------------------{x
These are the rules of Haven of the Embraced.  Read them, understand
them, worship them.
 
1: See the help pk file for Player Killing rules.
 
2: Your presence here is a privilege not a right. Obey any orders
   from gods, and you will be fine.  Deletion does not require a
   reason, appeals should be sent to Matthew alone.
 
3: Sitting around idle with a client is hazardous to your health.
   We may choose to disconnect or forcequit you for your own safety.
 
4: No multiple logins, multiple playing, or helping your own
   characters with other characters you own -- by any arrangment.
 
5: No kill stealing.  This means you cannot attack a mob someone else
   is fighting, unless they ask you to. Also avoid attacking fleeing
   mobs.
 
6: Cheating will not be tolerated.  This includes accepting favors
   from gods and exploiting bugs. If you find a bug, report it, then
   do not use it.
 
7: Changes to these rules are at the discretion of the immortals, and
   may be done without warning, notice, or even evidence of sanity.
 
8: On this mud, The Mad Hatter was god, is god, and will always be god. If he
   says something, it's law. If he decides something, accept it. If
   he rewards you, worship him. If he punishes you, be thankful he
   didn't do worse.
 
                Walk softly, and carry a big Stake.
{c---------------------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
pagea~
Message Boards
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
There are several message boards available.
 
News : is a message board from which you will see some
       In Character announcements.
Change : This message board is used to notify players
       of any changes that the coders implement into the
       mud.
Note : This is a player message board, you may send
       notes to everyone, or just one person.
Idea : This message board is used to submit ideas of
       things you would like to see put into Haven.
RpNote: This is message board is used for IC notes and
       global storylines.
 
See 'help note' for more information on how to use
the message boards.
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
pageb~
Frequently Asked Questions
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
Q:Where should I level?
A:Type {Carea{x for a list of areas for your level range.
 
Q:Where should I go for EQ(Equipment)?
A:Look through the different areas, explore and see what
  you find, that's really the only way to know. Many 
  players already know where to go, and some of them don't
  want to tell everyone where they found something. So
  spend some time exploring and looking around.
 
Q:Where can I get money?
A:By killing Mobiles(monsters) you usually recieve a random
  amount of money from the corpse. The players hoarde their
  money because it can be hard to accumulate massive amounts
  of money, and are reluctant to reveal the locations of
  good money spots.
 
Q:What happened to the spells?
A:Spells on Haven are known as Prayers, type Pray (prayername)
  to cast a prayer.
 
Q:What's the best Clan/Tribe/Tradition?
A:All of the coded affiliations each have distinct advantages
  and disadvantages, and as such we try to not have any one specific
  group or affiliation being better than any of the others.
 
Q:How many alts can I have?
A:You are allowed to have 4 alts on Haven, let's not confuse this
  with Multiplaying, which is logging on multiple characters at
  once, which is illegal.
 
Q:Does Haven have a webpage?
A:Haven does in fact have a webpage.  It also has a few other social
  media sites.  Check out {yhelp website{x for an updated list of Haven's
  social media and internet presence.

Q:I love this place!  How can I help it flourish?
A:Log in, play and learn about the MUD.  Spread the word to your friends.
  Submit ideas to the immortal staff.  We enjoy talking to our players
  and are more than willing to listen to constructive feedback.
{c---------------------------------------------------------------------{x
~
E
pagec~
{c-------------------------------------------------------{x
You must be bored, looking for pages that aren't supposed to
be here. Newbie Guide Book written by Sargoth Neevosaiden,
a.k.a. Maelstrome Neevosaiden.
 
I hope that you have found this guide useful, if you have
any questions please feel free to ask.

