#MPCODE
#250
Prelude Crossroads Guardian Greet~
if ispc $n
  mob echoat $n The guardian speaks: 'The city path to the east is for Vampires. The forest path to the west is for Humans.'
endif
~
#251
Prelude Sire Greet~
if race $n vampire
  mob echoat $n Your Sire greets you. 'Welcome to the shadows. First, type 'fangs' to extend them. Then 'kill vessel' to initiate combat, and type 'feed' while fighting!'
else
  mob echoat $n The city gates remain sealed to mortal blood.
  mob transfer $n 251
endif
~
#252
Prelude Gatekeeper Feeding Check~
if pblood $n >= 50
  mob echoat $n You may pass.
else
  mob echoat $n You must feed before proceeding.
  mob transfer $n 252
endif
~
#253
Prelude Discipline Master Check~
if disc $n potence >= 1
  mob echoat $n Excellent control of your disciplines.
else
  mob echoat $n You must use your discipline before proceeding.
  mob transfer $n 253
endif
~
#254
Prelude Sparring Dummy Fight~
if hpprc $n < 30
  mob echo The sparring dummy ceases its attack and flees!
  mob flee
  mob goto 250
endif
~
#255
Prelude Elder Vampire Graduation~
mob echoat $n 'Once you reach level 100, you can choose to Remort. This resets your level back to 1 but grants you additional Freebie points. True Blood mortals can Awaken as Mages or Garou, while Vampires and others gain increased capabilities through freebies.'
mob transfer $n 101
~
#256
Prelude Forest Ranger Greet~
if race $n human
  mob echoat $n Welcome to the forest. Type look and practice moving around.
else
  mob echoat $n The wild recoils from your undead presence.
  mob transfer $n 251
endif
~
#257
Prelude Grove Druid Greet~
mob echoat $n Here humans who prove worthy may Awaken as Werewolves (Garou) or Mages through the remort system.
~
#258
Prelude Skills Master Greet~
mob echoat $n Type 'practice', 'train', 'score', and 'cs' to manage your abilities.
~
#259
Prelude Remort Guide Graduation~
mob echoat $n 'Once you reach level 100, you can choose to Remort. This resets your level back to 1 but grants you additional Freebie points. True Blood mortals can Awaken as Mages or Garou, while Vampires and others gain increased capabilities through freebies.'
mob transfer $n 101
~
